# Self-improving loop trigger

When Wyatt's message begins with `loop:`, treat the remaining text as the task brief and run the saved self-improving workflow automatically. Do not ask Wyatt to repeat the setup or manually prepare the loop files.

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/BRIEFING.md`, the top of `docs/STATUS.md`, and the existing `.agent/self-improving/` files.
2. If this is a new card, preserve the old prompt and log, then prepare a fresh `prompt.md` and `log.md` for the new card. Keep one card at a time and protect unrelated work.
3. Make the first DeepSeek pass plan-only. Run the maker through the existing Cursor proxy with model `deepseek-v4-flash`:
   `python .agent/bin/deepseek_agent.py --role maker "$(Get-Content -Raw .agent/self-improving/prompt.md)"`
4. Perform Luna's watcher role without waiting for another instruction: read the run result and `watcher.md`, then append no more than 12 blunt lines to `log.md` using GOAL, KEPT, WASTED, FAILED, and NEXT.
5. Perform Sol's rewriter role without waiting for another instruction: read `prompt.md`, `log.md`, and `rewriter.md`; apply the latest NEXT note; update only the next prompt and append one change line to `log.md`.
6. Show Wyatt the resulting plan and stop for explicit `ack` before source edits. Do not commit, push, deploy, or delete files during the plan pass.
7. After `ack`, continue the maker -> Luna -> Sol cycle for the approved card. Apply the repository's normal QA and one-lever-per-commit rules. Stop after implementation and evidence unless Wyatt says `ship it`.
8. Treat `ship it` as separate deployment authorization. Run the required QA, push, deploy, and post-deploy checks only then. Never claim human playtest PASS without Wyatt's visual or playtest confirmation.

If the DeepSeek proxy or key is unavailable, report the exact setup error and stop. Never print or request the API key in chat.
